failed_call: a tool call that failed is a tool call rabadon has to see
  ok   - a successful call leaves exactly one move on the record
  ok   - a successful call records claimed_rc 0
  ok   - before the completion the move is open (claimed_rc -1)
  ok   - a failing call closes its move rather than opening a second one
  FAIL - the move is still open after the failure event — the completion was dropped
  FAIL - a failing call recorded NO err_sig ('') — the repeat detector cannot see it
  FAIL - failing call recorded claimed_rc=-1, expected 1
  FAIL - two identical failures did not share an err_sig: |
  ok   - the failing call opened a STEP_START on the ledger
  FAIL - STEP_START for the failing call was never closed — the blind spot is open
  FAIL - the closing event for a failing call is indistinguishable from a successful one
  ok   - a successful call carries no rc:1 (the marker is not painted on everything)
  ok   - the PreToolUse before a failure still exits 0
  ok   - observing a failed call exits 0 — it refuses nothing
  FAIL - rabadon installs no PostToolUseFailure hook — on a real machine the event is never delivered
  ok   - the live capture this suite is written against is in the repo
  FAIL - a silent failure recorded claimed_rc=-1, expected 1
  ok   - a silent failure honestly carries NO err_sig (nothing to sign)
  FAIL - a stale install is silently blind to failing calls — the card says nothing
  ok   - the card drops the blind spot once the install subscribes
  FAIL - the card was silenced by an event entry that has no rabadon hook in it
failed_call: 11 passed, 10 failed
